.TH "RTCERROR.SENTALERT" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCError.sentAlert \- RTCError: sentAlert property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]sentAlert\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]RTCError\f[R] interface specifies the DTLS alert number sent to
the remote peer, if the error represents an outbound DTLS error.
.SH VALUE
A positive integer value providing the DTLS alert number corresponding
to the DTLS error which was sent to the remote peer, as represented by
this \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] object.
This property is \f[CR]null\f[R] if \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] isn\(cqt
\f[CR]dtls\-failure\f[R].
